WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:01.817
Not enough leads coming in.

2
00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:05.617
You refresh the inbox,
and there's nothing new.

3
00:00:06.333 --> 00:00:11.283
So you try emailing new companies.
It usually goes wrong in four places.

4
00:00:11.967 --> 00:00:14.783
One. Nobody has the time for it.

5
00:00:15.567 --> 00:00:20.717
Two. Your emails land in spam,
and nobody tells you.

6
00:00:21.233 --> 00:00:26.617
Three. The list is old, so emails
bounce back or reach the wrong person.

7
00:00:27.567 --> 00:00:33.350
Four. Replies wait for days,
and people who said not now are forgotten.

8
00:00:35.733 --> 00:00:41.733
So we take the whole job off your hands.
It's called the Managed Outbound Channel.

9
00:00:42.767 --> 00:00:45.733
We find the right companies,
write to them,

10
00:00:45.733 --> 00:00:51.250
follow up, answer the replies,
and book the meetings into your calendar.

11
00:00:52.600 --> 00:00:56.350
Step one.
We agree who you want as customers.

12
00:00:56.667 --> 00:01:00.350
Each campaign gets one goal,
like reaching new companies,

13
00:01:00.467 --> 00:01:04.850
reviving old leads,
or finding more like your best customers.

14
00:01:05.767 --> 00:01:11.583
Step two. We set up separate inboxes
on web addresses like yours,

15
00:01:11.733 --> 00:01:14.283
so your main email stays safe.

16
00:01:15.567 --> 00:01:20.917
Each is set up so Gmail knows it's you,
then warmed up for three weeks,

17
00:01:20.933 --> 00:01:23.450
on an account used only for you.

18
00:01:24.667 --> 00:01:27.450
How much we send depends on what you need,

19
00:01:27.533 --> 00:01:32.217
from 18,000 emails a month
up to 80,000 or more.

20
00:01:33.433 --> 00:01:35.983
Step three. We search wide.

21
00:01:36.133 --> 00:01:39.600
Then an AI agent reads
each company's website,

22
00:01:39.600 --> 00:01:42.617
to check it's the kind you want,
before we look anyone up.

23
00:01:43.933 --> 00:01:48.867
Step four. We watch for a reason to write,
like a new hire,

24
00:01:48.867 --> 00:01:54.867
funding or a tender, so each first email
opens with a line meant only for them.

25
00:01:55.867 --> 00:01:56.867
Step five.

26
00:01:56.867 --> 00:02:00.983
Every address is checked, down to whether
the person still works there.

27
00:02:01.500 --> 00:02:06.383
If more than two in a hundred
would bounce, that list isn't sent.

28
00:02:07.233 --> 00:02:12.433
Step six. Three short emails in one week,
the third with a new angle.

29
00:02:12.433 --> 00:02:16.017
Then we stop,
or move to LinkedIn for the ones worth it.

30
00:02:16.500 --> 00:02:19.583
We test the wording one change at a time:

31
00:02:19.667 --> 00:02:23.817
subject lines, opening lines,
and what we ask them to do.

32
00:02:25.000 --> 00:02:26.550
Then someone replies.

33
00:02:28.233 --> 00:02:33.100
Step seven. Within a minute,
an AI agent reads the reply

34
00:02:33.100 --> 00:02:39.083
and sorts it: interested, a question,
not now, or an out-of-office.

35
00:02:39.467 --> 00:02:41.150
It's answered your way:

36
00:02:41.300 --> 00:02:46.383
book them straight in, ask your questions
first, or hand them to your team.

37
00:02:47.433 --> 00:02:50.817
At first, a person approves every reply.

38
00:02:51.000 --> 00:02:54.150
Quotes and contracts always go
to your team.

39
00:02:54.967 --> 00:02:58.533
Step eight.
The conversation carries on by email,

40
00:02:58.533 --> 00:03:02.117
LinkedIn, a call,
or WhatsApp once they've agreed.

41
00:03:02.733 --> 00:03:06.917
Our research travels with them,
so a brief is ready before the meeting:

42
00:03:07.167 --> 00:03:10.950
who they are, why we wrote,
and what to ask.

43
00:03:11.400 --> 00:03:16.483
And your CRM, where you keep track
of customers, fills itself in.

44
00:03:17.467 --> 00:03:20.800
Step nine. Meetings get booked,

45
00:03:20.800 --> 00:03:25.083
confirmed and reminded,
and no-shows get followed up.

46
00:03:25.867 --> 00:03:30.350
If someone says not now,
we note why and set a date,

47
00:03:30.367 --> 00:03:32.850
and the follow-up goes out by itself.

48
00:03:33.900 --> 00:03:37.717
Every month, one report: meetings held,

49
00:03:37.767 --> 00:03:43.317
qualified conversations, how many replied,
and what each meeting cost.

50
00:03:44.167 --> 00:03:48.217
Qualified means they fit,
they're interested,

51
00:03:48.400 --> 00:03:50.483
and they've confirmed a meeting.

52
00:03:51.200 --> 00:03:54.500
We don't track opens.
That needs a hidden tracker

53
00:03:54.500 --> 00:03:58.450
in every email,
and spam filters count it against you.

54
00:04:00.100 --> 00:04:06.050
We do our own outreach too.
Since August, nearly 3,000 emails,

55
00:04:06.267 --> 00:04:10.217
9 qualified conversations,
and 7 demos booked.

56
00:04:11.367 --> 00:04:17.217
One company ignored our first two emails.
The third got a reply in 55 minutes,

57
00:04:17.633 --> 00:04:20.483
then a call, then a demo booked.

58
00:04:21.433 --> 00:04:23.950
And the channel is sending by week four.

59
00:04:24.467 --> 00:04:29.350
A new sales hire usually takes
two to three months to get up to speed.

60
00:04:31.967 --> 00:04:36.483
We'll never promise you a number of leads,
replies or meetings.

61
00:04:37.000 --> 00:04:39.583
Judge us on whether
the work is done properly,

62
00:04:39.667 --> 00:04:41.650
and whether anybody got lost.

63
00:04:42.900 --> 00:04:47.017
Your part is small. Tell us who to reach,

64
00:04:47.200 --> 00:04:52.717
give us one hour on how you sell,
and name who takes the meetings.

65
00:04:53.000 --> 00:04:56.983
Then approve once a month,
and take the conversations.

66
00:04:57.767 --> 00:04:59.983
It starts with a thirty-minute call.

67
00:05:00.233 --> 00:05:05.017
If it's a fit, you get a written plan
within five working days,

68
00:05:05.033 --> 00:05:10.417
with the first ten companies we'd contact.
Free, and yours to keep.

69
00:05:11.367 --> 00:05:17.367
The Managed Outbound Channel, by Rheo AI.
Book your call on this page.

